In article <BwKy80.DHA@acsu.buffalo.edu>, v126hqpj@ubvmsb.cc.buffalo.edu (Philip S Piasecki) writes:
|> I have a question----I have an ancient computer and
|> I was wondering if you need a hard disk to play 
|> nethack, or can you play from two floppies.
|> 
|> Thanks!~
|> Phil

You don't _NEED_ a hard disk.  But it won't work on two floppies either.
You need either a hard drive or a 1.44M or 2.88M 3.5" disk.

BTW:  The 1.44 will fill up quickly with level files, so you won't be able to
get very deep (lv 15 or so) before the disk fills up and the dungeon collapses.
